Q: Absent Load barrier what can go wrong on a processor that reoderes loads?
A: Well the loads could execute in the wrong order but mainly because of 3 reasons:
   --> Processor can do load speculation as Sarita pointed out
       http://www.cs.umd.edu/~pugh/java/memoryModel/archive/0053.html

   --> Processor can maintain cache coherence but process invalidate requests from
       remote writes behind cache read requsts as Dan Scales pointed out.
       http://www.cs.umd.edu/~pugh/java/memoryModel/archive/0055.html

   --> Of course if the processors dont have coherent caches then this is definitely possible.
       <where you can have multiple cache line owners in X state>

[UPDATE] There are differences between Address Dependent Load reordering and Data Dependent
         Load reordering. This document talks about the former. Only ALPHA to the best of my 
	 knowledge does this kind of reordering. All others like PowerPC ARM do the latter.

